  "step_3": "The decision reason requires consideration of variance, which involves both outcomes and their squared deviations from the mean. However, the individual only refers to the probability of winning, noting that it is doubled in Lottery B. They do not reference outcome magnitudes in relation to variability, nor do they indicate any calculation or conceptual use of variance. The justification is purely probability-focused and does not align with the rule of minimizing variance. While both lotteries have the same expected value (6 Euros), the individual does not mention this either, further suggesting a simple heuristic based on probability of winning. Therefore, there is no evidence that the individual used variance as a decision criterion.",
